riscv64 zkVM: fix two Checked-JIT-only assertions in earlier perf patches

Release JITs were unaffected (codegen and the guest's outputs are unchanged), but a Checked
JIT - needed for JitDump/inlining diagnostics - aborted on either of these:

- perf-50 marked the GPR temps of an unrolled Memmove delay-free to keep them off the
  address registers. The temps' defs precede the address uses at the same location, so
  LSRA already allocates them while those registers are busy, and a block store has no
  def at the next location for a delayed free to wait on: "Found a delayRegFree
  associated with Location with no reference".
- The integer Math.Min/Max (Zbb) build asserted both operands have the node's exact
  type and that the node is 64-bit; 32-bit forms reach it, and perf-40 may contain a
  widening cast of an operand. Only the integral kind is asserted now.

diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/lsrariscv64.cpp b/src/coreclr/jit/lsrariscv64.cpp
index ec17b7198..44f703c52 100644
--- a/src/coreclr/jit/lsrariscv64.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/lsrariscv64.cpp
@@ -430,11 +430,12 @@ int LinearScan::BuildNode(GenTree* tree)
                 case NI_System_Math_Max:
                 case NI_System_Math_MinUnsigned:
                 case NI_System_Math_MaxUnsigned:
+                    // Both 32- and 64-bit forms reach here, and a widening cast of an operand may be
+                    // contained (perf-40), so only the integral kind is checked.
                     assert(m_compiler->compOpportunisticallyDependsOn(InstructionSet_Zbb));
                     assert(op2 != nullptr);
-                    assert(op2->TypeIs(tree->TypeGet()));
-                    assert(op1->TypeIs(tree->TypeGet()));
-                    assert(tree->TypeIs(TYP_I_IMPL));
+                    assert(varTypeIsIntegral(op1) && varTypeIsIntegral(op2));
+                    assert(varTypeIsIntegral(tree));
                     break;
 
                 // Operand and its result must be integers
@@ -1322,8 +1323,10 @@ int LinearScan::BuildBlockStore(GenTreeBlk* blkNode)
                 // (a remainder is covered by an overlapping 8-byte access), two GPRs for
                 // a 3..7 byte block (two overlapping accesses), one for 1/2/4 bytes. The
                 // size is capped by getUnrollThreshold(Memmove) at MaxInternalCount * 8.
-                // The temps must not alias the address registers, which stay live across
-                // the loads: delay-free them.
+                // The temps cannot alias the address registers: their defs precede the
+                // address uses at this location, so they are allocated while those are
+                // still busy. They are not delay-freed - a store has no def at the next
+                // location for a delayed free to wait on (LSRA asserts on that).
                 assert(size > 0);
                 unsigned temps;
                 if (size >= REGSIZE_BYTES)
@@ -1339,7 +1342,6 @@ int LinearScan::BuildBlockStore(GenTreeBlk* blkNode)
                 {
                     buildInternalIntRegisterDefForNode(blkNode);
                 }
-                setInternalRegsDelayFree = true;
                 break;
             }
 
